%% NOTE: This diagram is superseded by lmcache-ipu-pull-model-flow.mmd
%% which covers both Store and Retrieve in one combined diagram.
%% Kept for Falcon-level naming detail only.

sequenceDiagram
    participant vLLM as vLLM / Bench Tool<br/>(Initiator Xeon)
    participant F_I as MMG-400 Falcon<br/>(Initiator)
    participant WIRE as 400GbE
    participant F_T as MMG-400 Falcon<br/>(KV Cache Node)
    participant LMC as LMCache Server<br/>(KV Cache Node Xeon)
    participant DRAM as Registered DRAM<br/>(L1)
    participant SSD as NVMe Gen5<br/>(L2)

    Note over vLLM,SSD: Pull Model: Target controls when and where data arrives

    vLLM->>vLLM: DMA: GPU HBM → host DRAM, fence
    vLLM->>vLLM: IPURdmaWrapper.wrap()<br/>→ (rkey, addr, len=256KB)
    vLLM->>LMC: write intent [ZMQ ctrl, 128B]<br/>(hash, rkey, addr, len)

    Note over vLLM: NO data crosses the wire yet.<br/>Only a 128B control message.

    LMC->>LMC: Admission check: duplicate?

    alt DRAM full
        LMC->>SSD: async flush evicted page (io_uring)
        Note over SSD: fire-and-forget
        LMC->>DRAM: free evicted slot
    end

    LMC->>DRAM: allocate 256KB page at addr Y

    Note over LMC: TARGET DECIDES WHEN TO PULL

    LMC->>F_T: post RDMA Read descriptor<br/>(src=initiator:addr, dst=Y, 256KB)
    F_T->>WIRE: RDMA Read Request (64B)
    WIRE->>F_I: RDMA Read Request

    Note over F_I: Falcon serves autonomously:<br/>DMA gather from host DRAM<br/>(Initiator Xeon NOT involved)

    F_I->>WIRE: RDMA Read Response (256KB)
    WIRE->>F_T: 256KB arrives
    F_T->>DRAM: DMA scatter to addr Y (256KB)

    Note over F_T: Falcon signals completion

    F_T->>LMC: completion doorbell
    LMC->>DRAM: update hash table (key → addr Y)
    LMC->>vLLM: store complete ACK [ZMQ ctrl]

    Note over F_I,F_T: Data path: Falcon-to-Falcon, zero CPU copy<br/>Initiator Xeon: wrap() + send intent (done before pull)<br/>KV Cache Xeon: admission + alloc + post descriptor + index
